# Tech Theme UI

The workbench uses the **tech theme**: solid surfaces, hairline borders, no blur, no refraction — the visual language of Cursor, ChatGPT, and Claude Code.

> The previous Apple Liquid Glass system is **deprecated**. Do not add `backdrop-filter`, `--glass-*` tokens, or `GlassLens`/`GlassPanelShell` refraction to any new UI. The `GlassLens`/`GlassPanelShell` components that remain are inert pass-through wrappers.

## Rule #1: Tech tokens only

Use `--tech-*` tokens for every surface, border, text color, and shadow. Never hardcode hex values in CSS modules.

| Layer | Token | Value (dark) |
|-------|-------|--------------|
| App background | `--tech-bg-canvas` | `#181818` |
| Chrome (title / side / terminal) | `--tech-bg-chrome` | `#141414` |
| Side panels / nav | `--tech-bg-side-panel` | `#141414` |
| Elevated cards | `--tech-bg-elevated` | `#1c1c1c` |
| Hover / muted | `--tech-bg-muted` | `#222222` |
| Border | `--tech-border` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` |
| Border (strong) | `--tech-border-strong` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.16)` |
| Primary text | `--tech-text-primary` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.92)` |
| Accent | `--tech-accent` | `#4c7dff` |

Full list in `projectos/workbench/src/styles/tokens.css`.

## Rule #2: No glass

```css
/* ✅ Correct — solid surface, hairline border */
.panel {
  background: var(--tech-bg-side-panel);
  border-right: 1px solid var(--tech-border);
}

/* ❌ Never — no backdrop-filter, no glass tokens, no blur */
.panel {
  background: var(--glass-bg-clear);
  backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur-lg));
}
```

## Utility classes

`projectos/workbench/src/styles/global.css` provides:

| Class | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `.tech-surface` | Elevated card with border + subtle shadow |
| `.tech-surface-hover` | Adds hover transition to `.tech-surface` |
| `.tech-nav` | Side-panel / nav chrome |
| `.tech-card` | Content card, 6px radius |
| `.tech-button-primary` / `.tech-button-secondary` | Button styles |
| `.tech-focus` | Visible focus ring (`:focus-visible`) |
| `.tech-no-glass` | Force-remove any residual glass effect |

## Radius

Small radius everywhere: `4px` controls, `6px` cards/buttons, `8px` overlays. Do not use `--radius-glass-*` values (14–34px) for new UI.

## Shadows

Subtle and few. Use `--tech-shadow-sm` (panels), `--tech-shadow-md` (floating cards), `--tech-shadow-lg` (modals). Focus ring: `--tech-shadow-focus`.

## Motion

- Micro-interactions: 150–300ms with `--ease-out`.
- No infinite decorative animations.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Accessibility

- `:focus-visible` → `box-shadow: var(--tech-shadow-focus)` on all interactive elements.
- Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 on `--tech-bg-*` surfaces.
- Icon-only buttons: `aria-label` required.

## Legacy

Old glass utility classes (`.glass-nav`, `.glass-elevated`, …) still exist in `global.css` for reference but are no longer applied by any component. Do not use them.
